{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.PlancherelRestrictionIncoherent","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.PlancherelRestrictionIncoherent","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FinCases","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.PlancherelRestriction.not_coherent_of_pos_of_ne_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.PlancherelRestriction.not_coherent_of_pos_of_ne_one","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PlancherelRestrictionIncoherent.lean#L112-L131","doc":"**For real `q > 0`, the Plancherel weights are restriction-coherent only at `q = 1`.**\nSo for `q > 0`, `q ≠ 1`, no trace family on `H_3 ⊂ H_4` — no Markov trace at any\nparameter — carries quantum-Plancherel weights at both levels. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.PlancherelRestriction.coherent_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.PlancherelRestriction.coherent_iff","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PlancherelRestrictionIncoherent.lean#L82-L110","doc":"**Restriction coherence holds iff `[3]_q · (q − q⁻¹)⁴ = 0`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.PlancherelRestriction.Coherent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.PlancherelRestriction.Coherent","kind":"def","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PlancherelRestrictionIncoherent.lean#L78-L80","doc":"The `n = 4` Plancherel weights restrict to a multiple of the `n = 3` ones. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.PlancherelRestriction.restrict","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.PlancherelRestriction.restrict","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PlancherelRestrictionIncoherent.lean#L72-L76","doc":"Restriction of the `n = 4` weights to `n = 3` by the branching rule. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.PlancherelRestriction.w3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.PlancherelRestriction.w3","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PlancherelRestrictionIncoherent.lean#L66-L70","doc":"Per-character Plancherel weights `d_q(μ)² / f^μ` on `μ ⊢ 3` (unnormalised). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.PlancherelRestriction.w4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.PlancherelRestriction.w4","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PlancherelRestrictionIncoherent.lean#L58-L64","doc":"Per-character Plancherel weights `d_q(λ)² / f^λ` on `λ ⊢ 4` (unnormalised). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.PlancherelRestriction.b4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.PlancherelRestriction.b4","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PlancherelRestrictionIncoherent.lean#L56-L56","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.PlancherelRestriction.b3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"